1. What is SharePoint?

    SharePoint Online is Microsoft's cloud platform for storing, organizing, sharing, securing, and collaborating on 
    business information and documents.
    
    A company can use it for:
        Company intranet
        Team/project sites
        Document storage and collaboration
        Business data in Lists
        Approval processes
        Knowledge/document management
        Secure file sharing
        Power Apps / Power Automate solutions

""""SharePoint is primarily used by people in the organization, but external people can also be given access if external sharing is enabled."""

Main Components:
Concept                       What it means
Site                      Workspace/container
List                    Structured business data
ListItem                    One record in a list
Columns                    Fields of a list
Document             LibraryStores documents/files
Folder                    Organizes files
File                    Word, Excel, PDF, etc.
Page                         UI/content page
Web                     PartComponent placed on a page
Content                 TypeReusable definition for types of content
Permissions                Controls access
Groups                Groups of users for permissions
Views                Different ways of showing list/library information
SPFx                    Framework for custom SharePoint development
